{"description":"GitHub issue maleolabs/eka-cli#28 (bug, medium, source: agent, EKA 1.2.0): the eka_new MCP tool intermittently refuses with 'new requires {project, namespace, type, id}' although all required params are present; a byte-identical retry succeeds. Failing calls carried ~2-4KB unicode-heavy content payloads.\n\nVerified against source (eka-mcp worktree feat/sto-mcp-capability-expansion):\n- The refusal is emitted at ONE condition in internal/mcp/server.go callTool case \"new\": json.Unmarshal(args, \u0026p) error OR empty required string field - one schema-shaped message conflating THREE distinct causes: (1) malformed/truncated JSON arguments, (2) missing field, (3) present-but-empty or wrong-typed field.\n- The MCP server request path is deterministic and single-goroutine (transport.go newline-delimited stdio, 64MiB cap, reassembly correct; fuzz-hardened; no shared mutable state). Therefore a byte-identical retry succeeding PROVES the server received different bytes the first time - the nondeterminism is upstream of HandleMessage (client/transport side).\n- Go's encoding/json does not reject unicode/lone surrogates, so unicode per se cannot trip the parser; byte length is the plausible discriminator.\n- Contract drift: the reported 1.2.0 message enforces FOUR fields {project,namespace,type,id}, but no local ref contains that message (git pickaxe over all refs) while the tool schema advertises only {type,id} as required and tools_test.go names all four. The deployed binary differs from repo source.\n\nRanked hypotheses: H1 client-side serialization/truncation of large multibyte payloads breaking the stdio line framing (most likely, size-correlated); H2 schema/binary drift causing deterministic refusal when the model omits project/namespace under large-content generation pressure; H3 double-encoded or wrongly-typed arguments.\n\nFix direction: make the refusal accurate (per-cause messages), align schema with enforcement, add refusal-time argument byte-length diagnostics; do NOT chase a unicode parsing fix (decoder does not reject unicode).","impact":"","acceptanceCriteria":"- Refusal at the eka_new tool entry discriminates its three causes: JSON parse failure surfaces the sanitized decoder error; missing field names WHICH field is absent; empty/wrong-typed field names the field.\n- inputSchema `required` list aligned with actual enforcement in callTool (no contract drift between advertised schema and runtime check).\n- Argument byte-length logged (stderr diagnostics) on every identity-shaped refusal, to discriminate client-side truncation from param omission.\n- Regression tests cover all three refusal causes plus a large (~4KB) unicode-heavy content payload.\n- Root cause of the intermittency identified and documented (client-side truncation vs omitted params vs double-encoded args); deployed 1.2.0 binary reconciled with repo source (4-field vs 2-field message discrepancy explained).\n- Review findings posted as a comment on maleolabs/eka-cli#28; issue closed only after the fix ships in a release."}